{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4546","id":4734433645,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGjG5bQ","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4546","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4546.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4546.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4546","number":4546,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A29: fuzz HTTP stream limits, cancellation and cleanup","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.8\nRelated: #1150; follows merged #4543.\n\n## Actual transport behavior\nExtend the network adapter with nine closed cases using the public HttpTransport and native fetch against one fixture-owned loopback origin. This exercises the production request/response path in addition to policy parsing and native-host authorization.\n\nThe cases verify exact 32-byte responses and POST requests, split UTF-8 response streaming, 201/404 status and filtered headers, announced Content-Length overflow before any body is supplied, chunked overflow without a partial result, request overflow before transmission, cancellation after actual arrival, and a real finite timeout distinct from cancellation.\n\nInputs select reviewed checks and bounded variants. Each case allows two transport calls, at most two server requests and four connections; headers, bodies, output and timers are bounded. The fixture retains transport statistics and server byte counts, then checks closure of jobs, sockets, server and timers. Unexpected errors propagate. Combined network seeds remain within the 32-seed ceiling.\n\n## Validation\n- 47 focused tests passed: 13 HTTP cases plus existing native-host and text-target regressions.\n- Command: `node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap tests/conformance/fuzz/http-transport-target.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/native-host-target.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/text-targets.test.js`.\n- Node 24.19.0, Linux x64; tested local commit `050caf59d685d007927fce86b79e278da9f72cfc`, tree `f23153c526230956a4f2623fa3e239508477da7a`.\n- Published tree verified byte-identical; the published parent maps to the identical tested native-host parent tree. GitHub-created commit metadata differs.\n- Independent lifecycle, authority and source review passed. Existing A29 manifest covers the new test.\n\nThis qualifies the recorded bounded local cases. Provider, native SDK and affected-engine/platform qualification remains separate; ordinary core runs static/build checks without Node tests.","created_at":"2026-10-04T12:41:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T12:42:25Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T12:42:25Z","merged_at":"2026-10-04T12:42:25Z","merge_commit_sha":"bf85020e6024cdd679a0234d9f050ca7dedddf53","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12525232279,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU59Ms88AAAAC6o_glw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/label